%I A267295 #25 Nov 10 2026 16:47:55
%S A267295 3,6,9,14,17,22,27,36,39,46,49,58
%N A267295 Circulant Ramsey numbers RC_2(3,n) of the second kind.
%C A267295 The smallest number a(n), such that any triangle-free cyclic (also known as circulant) graph with at least a(n) vertices has independence number at least n. The terminology and the terms given here are from Harborth and Krause (2003); however, in another form, essentially they were considered and partly calculated already by Kalbfleich in 1965.
%C A267295 Moreover, the sequence is related to the ordinary two-color Ramsey numbers R(3,n), given in A000791, by the relation a(n) <= A000791(n) for all n, as proved by Kalbfleisch. This inequality is known to be strict for 6 <= n <= 8, and for n = 10.
%C A267295 a(13) = R_C(3,13) = 58 was established by Coniglio et al. (2026); see A000789 for an independent exhaustive confirmation. The upper bound a(13) <= 58 also follows from Kuznetsov's enumeration of distance colorings. - _Benjamin Schippers_, Nov 03 2026
%D A267295 H. Harborth, S. Krause: Ramsey Numbers for Circulant Colorings, Congressus Numerantium 161 (2003), 139-150.
%H A267295 Stefano Coniglio, Fabio Furini, Ivana Ljubić, Pablo San Segundo, Johannes Thüerauf, and Emiliano Traversi, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.18769">An Integer Programming Approach to Compute Lower Bounds for Ramsey Numbers Using Circulant Graphs</a>, arXiv:2608.18769 [math.OC], 2026.
%H A267295 J. G. Kalbfleisch, <a href="https://doi.org/10.4153/CMB-1965-041-7">Construction of special edge-chromatic graphs</a>, Canad. Math. Bull., 8 (1965), 575-584.
%H A267295 Eugene Kuznetsov, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1505.07186">Computational lower limits on small Ramsey numbers</a>, arXiv:1505.07186 [cs.DM], 2015-2016.
%H A267295 <a href="/index/Ra#Ramsey numbers">Index entries for sequences related to Ramsey numbers</a>
%F A267295 a(n) = A000789(n)+1 and a(n) >= A267296(n) for all n.
%Y A267295 Cf. A000789, A000791, A267296.
%K A267295 nonn,hard,more,changed
%O A267295 2,1
%A A267295 _Jörgen Backelin_, Jan 12 2016
%E A267295 a(13) from _Benjamin Schippers_, Nov 03 2026
